//
// The LM-head GEMV's re-execution gate. `[2026-08-21]` The 19 x 8192
// `lm_head_gemv` multi-launch ELF that shipped until this morning returned
// wrong, non-deterministic values in partition 0 whenever it executed
// immediately after itself (doc 57 section 1.4/1.5, devq 446-448, 452, 458:
// 5 of 7 dispatches wrong, healed only by running another ELF in between, NOT
// by a 0.5 s idle). Production decode never places the head next to itself
// and `make verify` judges token sets, so neither could see it; this gate
// compiles the production builder's module fresh and dispatches it seven
// times in the patterns that expose it.
//
// `[2026-08-21, 03:40]` The production head became 9 x 16384 + 4480 (mixed
// partitions, m_input 8; doc 57 section 5 item 5b) and this gate went 7 / 7
// clean on it (devq 482, 484) -- the XFAIL that stood for the 19 x 8192 form
// is gone and the gate is now a regression guard: a builder or compiler
// change that brings the re-execution family back (doc 57 section 1.5's
// seven-row table -- it is NOT understood, only avoided) turns this red.
// The 19 x 8192 reproducer lives on in the evidence root's probes.
//
// No HF weights: random weights against an f32 reference. NPU serialization
// lives one layer down (KernelCache takes /tmp/npu.lock).
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_npu2_lm_head_reexec
// RUN: cd test_npu2_lm_head_reexec
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile check-lm-head-reexec PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s
//
// CHECK: [reexec] d1 first dispatch: clean
// CHECK: [reexec] d2 back-to-back: clean
// CHECK: [reexec] d3 back-to-back: clean
// CHECK: [reexec] d4 after 0.5 s idle: clean
// CHECK: [reexec] d5 new input back-to-back: clean
// CHECK: [reexec] d6 after other ELF: clean
// CHECK: [reexec] d7 back-to-back after d6: clean
// CHECK: [reexec] PASS
